---
# The pull job's private key, from the SOPS key pi_peer_backup_ssh_key. The CronJob projects
# this Secret and pi-peer-backup-ssh into one volume at /ssh, so the script still reads
# /ssh/id.
#
# A Secret of its own because the value is a multi-line PEM block: Flux strips every newline
# from a substituted value, so no `${...}` placeholder can carry it, and D3 ships this Secret
# as a SOPS-encrypted manifest instead (target slice R2, PR 6). `render_sops_manifests` in
# defaults/main.yml names this file, so a placeholder render leaves it out. `to_json` writes
# the stored key as one double-quoted scalar, newlines escaped, and keeps its final newline
# only if the stored value has one.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: pi-peer-backup-ssh-key
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
type: Opaque
stringData:
  id: {{ pi_peer_backup_ssh_key | to_json }}
